language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session1_money_change: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Alice has to give Bob some change. She has different types of coins of different values, and a certain
$ number of coins of each type available. Compose the change from the available coins so that the number of coins used is
$ as small as possible.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `session1_money_change.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session1_money_change.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `session1_money_change_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py session1_money_change.json
$   savilerow model.eprime session1_money_change_1.param -run-solver

$ amount: the amount of change to give, in the same units as the coin values
given amount : int(0..)
$ types_of_coins_dim1: the number of coin types (derived from the data)
given types_of_coins_dim1 : int
$ types_of_coins[i]: the value of coin type i (indices from 1)
given types_of_coins : matrix indexed by [int(1..types_of_coins_dim1)] of int(1..)
$ available_coins[i]: the number of coins of type i that Alice has
given available_coins : matrix indexed by [int(1..types_of_coins_dim1)] of int(0..)

$ coin_counts[i]: the number of coins of type i given to Bob (indices from 1)
find coin_counts : matrix indexed by [int(1..types_of_coins_dim1)] of int(0..amount)

minimising (sum i : int(1..types_of_coins_dim1) . coin_counts[i])
such that
$ Alice cannot give more coins of a type than she has
forAll i : int(1..types_of_coins_dim1) . coin_counts[i] <= available_coins[i],
$ the coins given add up to the amount of change
(sum i : int(1..types_of_coins_dim1) . coin_counts[i] * types_of_coins[i]) = amount
